
docs/requirements.md:845-882
845:## NFR-BDC-0001: In-process get latency
846:
847:**Status:** Approved
848:
849:An in-process cached `get` takes under 1 ms when at most `READ_DATING_THRESHOLD` (2000) undated journal entries exist and no foreign writer holds the write lock. The one `get` that dates a larger burst, and gets while a foreign writer holds the lock over more than 2000 undated entries, are bounded excursions recorded in ADR-STORE-0004 (lead rulings S26 and S31).
850:
851:**Source:** baseline design, Performance
852:
853:## NFR-BDC-0002: CLI get latency
854:
855:**Status:** Approved
856:
857:A new-process CLI `get` takes under 50 ms.
858:
859:**Source:** baseline design, Performance
860:
861:## NFR-BDC-0003: Incremental sync time
862:
863:**Status:** Approved
864:
865:An incremental sync of a 1000-bead phase takes under 1 s.
866:
867:**Source:** baseline design, Performance
868:
869:## NFR-BDC-0004: bd calls bounded by the deadline
870:
871:**Status:** Approved
872:
873:Each `bd` call has a 30 s timeout and is capped at the time left before the caller's deadline, so a tick never exceeds its budget.
874:
875:**Source:** baseline design, Performance (drain bounds), Open items
876:
877:## NFR-BDC-0005: Unit tests without bd
878:
879:**Status:** Approved
880:
881:Unit tests run with no `bd` and no dolt, using a deterministic fake runner; each ported test fails against at least one of the planted bugs listed in the baseline design.
882:

