docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-1-runtime-migration.md:620-664
620:### QA8 inventory budget correction (FTQ-011)
621:
622:QA8's exact report is
623:https://github.com/randlee/beads-cache/pull/108#issuecomment-6622741614.
624:The retained developer lifecycle run failed 14/15 and the independent Rust QA8
625:run failed 13/15 with owned inventory timeouts. Both original logs remain under
626:`.cursor/qa-evidence/phase-c/c-1/qa-8/logs/`; the focused later pass does not erase
627:either failure. They establish the actual helper timing dependency, without
628:establishing a particular slow invocation, PID or host-load cause.
629:
630:The test-only inventory now consumes its caller's remaining absolute budget;
631:there is no separate 50ms cap or minimum 50ms slice. Preflight retains its 250ms
632:allowance. Diagnostic/readiness callers supply their existing absolute observation
633:or fixture deadline, capped by the five-second fixture lifetime. Cleanup retains
634:the same initial 100ms drain, absolute 250ms quiescence boundary and absolute
635:one-second final boundary. No phase or fixture timeout is renewed after error.
636:Every started inventory owns its child and output file and completes or is
637:killed and actually reaped, including output/parse errors and assertion unwind.
638:An empty or incomplete inventory is never evidence of session emptiness.
639:
640:A transient scan error may recover only with fresh complete evidence before the
641:same phase deadline. Failed scans reset the stable-census observation. Cleanup
642:requires two complete stable stopped-session censuses, the actual root wait,
643:and a fresh complete empty-session census after that join, including the root.
644:Exhausting any required proof remains an error even if a later diagnostic sees
645:an empty session. The preliminary drain may recover through those required
646:proofs; recovery is logged while the original fixture failure/timeout is retained.
647:The one-attempt handoff to the shared supervisor remains: error, Drop and a
648:second cleanup call cannot start a fresh registry or session cleanup budget.
649:Pre-registration ownership, in-flight launch closure, Linux raw nonpositive SID
650:filtering and identity rechecks are preserved.
651:
652:Deterministic added regressions self-stop and acknowledge an actual owned
653:inventory command, then resume it after 80ms under the existing preflight and
654:cleanup budgets. Another injects a transient census error while retaining a real
655:failed fixture exit. A genuine noncooperative command consumes the existing
656:cleanup phases, is killed/reaped each time, and leaves the failed receipt false
657:after root reaping, a repeated cleanup call, Drop and a separate diagnostic audit.
658:The existing true timeout/unwind inventory proof now acknowledges the command's
659:kernel stop before testing it. These are test inputs, not host tuning or new
660:process-control promises.
